  "title": "The Spiral Library Return",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "block-world chain reactions",
  "premise": "A block librarian wants to return a ring of oversized books to shelves, but the aisle is too narrow for a cart. Each shelving tray rotates into an empty position and frees the next tray, circulating one vacancy around the ring until all books land beside their matching symbols.",
  "hook": "We only have one empty space.",
  "visible_action": "One empty tray rotates; books travel in a ring; shelf symbols line up; the vacancy returns to its original bay.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "An empty position can be a useful resource in a constrained sequence.",
  "gate": "Fictional rotating shelf model; validate every intermediate clearance before rendering the mechanism.",
